      "message": "One thing that struck me as a possible foot gun was the free-form sksl declaration sans layout for the variables. The RenderStep declarations are all able to use enum types so that the sksl is entirely constructed dynamically. \n\nBut I also don\u0027t see a simple solution to being able to statically declare struct definitions in C++ that would just be converted to the sksl you can write directly. Assuming we don\u0027t need reflection based on these struct definitions down the road, I think this is a fine solution that balances automatic assembly with C++ overhead.",
